UNIT-DRIVER PARITY
==================

Each ported leaf module gets:
  parity/drivers/<module>.f   fixed-input Fortran driver, stdout only
  parity/golden/<module>.txt  captured from the pinned rebuilt baseline
  a #[test] in the Rust module that emits the same text format

The driver is compiled directly with the original Fortran source and the
pinned flags, for example:

  gfortran -O0 -ffp-contract=off -fno-fast-math -std=legacy -fdec \
    -o /tmp/dcross_drv parity/drivers/dcross.f vendor/nastran95/mis/dcross.f
  /tmp/dcross_drv > /tmp/dcross.out
  diff -u parity/golden/dcross.txt /tmp/dcross.out

No dates, timing, memory addresses, or uninitialized values in driver output.
The golden is committed. The diff must be empty.

The 64-deck qualified corpus is guarded by tools/qualify.sh.
